{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794531686181,"sessionID":"ses_e2d9477baffetZHrT79yuj36Es","part":{"partID":"prt_1d26c7183001i73jC0uRnM6hBb","sessionID":"ses_e2d9477baffetZHrT79yuj36Es","messageID":"msg_1d26c6572001fr1ULtm7jYFkxm","type":"tool","id":"call_24c9a97647ea4f1abf1350b4","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/AGENTS.md","offset":50,"limit":30},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/AGENTS.md, lines 50-79\n50: 2. Classify intent: Research or Implementation\n51: 3. Parse the request; judge confidence against the Confidence Thresholds below — the single scale, no second one.\n52: 4. Below the proceed bar → INVESTIGATE (max 3 iterations) → ESCALATE per §7.\n53: \n54: #### Confidence Thresholds\n55: \n56: | Confidence | Action |\n57: | --- | --- |\n58: | **≥80%** | Proceed with citable source |\n59: | **40-79%** | Proceed with caveats |\n60: | **<40%** | Ask for clarification or mark \"UNKNOWN\" |\n61: | **Override** | Blockers/conflicts → ask regardless of score |\n62: \n63: #### GATE 2: SKILL ROUTING [REQUIRED for non-trivial tasks]\n64: 1. A) Primary: use the Skill Advisor Hook brief the runtime surfaced, when present. See `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`.\n65: 2. B) Direct call: run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"[request]\"}' --format json` when no hook brief is present or when diagnosing hook behavior.\n66: 3. C) Cite user's explicit direction: \"User specified: [exact quote]\"\n67: - Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed\n68: - **Artifact trigger — binds on what you write, regardless of the advisor score.** Before the FIRST code write, route through `sk-code`. Before the FIRST `.md` write, route through `sk-doc`, except spec-folder docs (`system-spec-kit`'s) and the gitignored runtime state Gate 3 exempts, which no skill owns. Routing means loading what its ROUTER.md resolves, per Gate 5's loading rule. A skill already in context is not re-read. A resolved contract wrong for this case is followed and amended, per PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK step 4.\n69: - Output: `SKILL ROUTING: [result]` or `SKILL ROUTING: User directed → [name]`; when the artifact trigger fires, add `ARTIFACT: [skill] → [what its router resolved]`\n70: - Skip: trivial queries only (greetings, single-line questions). The artifact trigger skips only the §6 exemption class.\n71: \n72: #### GATE 3: SPEC FOLDER QUESTION [HARD] BLOCK — ASKED FIRST\n73: **Fires when** the turn will write a file — creating, editing, deleting, moving, or generating one — or will write continuity state (a save, a resume, a further iteration). **Does not fire** when the request is purely read-only: review, audit, inspect, analyze, explain, standing alone, or when its only write is gitignored runtime state under `.skilled/skills/.state/`. A read-only word next to a write trigger does not disqualify it.\n74: \n75: - **Machine contract:** `system-spec-kit/shared/gate-3-classifier.ts` (`classifyPrompt()`) owns the exact vocabulary; the sentence above paraphrases it.\n76: - **Options (stable labels, recommend one), asked via the `communication-handoff.md` §5 tool:**\n77:   - **A) Existing** - Continue in the detected/current spec or its current phase child when the work fits that scope. **Reply with the folder path.**\n78:   - **B) New** - Create a new top-level packet only when no existing packet suits the work. Decide independently whether it is standard or phased. **Reply with a new folder path.**\n79:   - **C) Related** - Use another existing packet, a child of an existing phase parent, a related standard packet split into phases once it meets both thresholds independently, or a series parent for a different change to the same artifact as an existing same-track packet. **Reply with the folder or child path.**\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 80]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/AGENTS.md, lines 50-79\n50: 2. Classify intent: Research or Implementation\n51: 3. Parse the request; judge confidence against the Confidence Thresholds below — the single scale, no second one.\n52: 4. Below the proceed bar → INVESTIGATE (max 3 iterations) → ESCALATE per §7.\n53: \n54: #### Confidence Thresholds\n55: \n56: | Confidence | Action |\n57: | --- | --- |\n58: | **≥80%** | Proceed with citable source |\n59: | **40-79%** | Proceed with caveats |\n60: | **<40%** | Ask for clarification or mark \"UNKNOWN\" |\n61: | **Override** | Blockers/conflicts → ask regardless of score |\n62: \n63: #### GATE 2: SKILL ROUTING [REQUIRED for non-trivial tasks]\n64: 1. A) Primary: use the Skill Advisor Hook brief the runtime surfaced, when present. See `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`.\n65: 2. B) Direct call: run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"[request]\"}' --format json` when no hook brief is present or when diagnosing hook behavior.\n66: 3. C) Cite user's explicit direction: \"User specified: [exact quote]\"\n67: - Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed\n68: - **Artifact trigger — binds on what you write, regardless of the advisor score.** Before the FIRST code write, route through `sk-code`. Before the FIRST `.md` write, route through `sk-doc`, except spec-folder docs (`system-spec-kit`'s) and the gitignored runtime state Gate 3 exempts, which no skill owns. Routing means loading what its ROUTER.md resolves, per Gate 5's loading rule. A skill already in context is not re-read. A resolved contract wrong for this case is followed and amended, per PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK step 4.\n69: - Output: `SKILL ROUTING: [result]` or `SKILL ROUTING: User directed → [name]`; when the artifact trigger fires, add `ARTIFACT: [skill] → [what its router resolved]`\n70: - Skip: trivial queries only (greetings, single-line questions). The artifact trigger skips only the §6 exemption class.\n71: \n72: #### GATE 3: SPEC FOLDER QUESTION [HARD] BLOCK — ASKED FIRST\n73: **Fires when** the turn will write a file — creating, editing, deleting, moving, or generating one — or will write continuity state (a save, a resume, a further iteration). **Does not fire** when the request is purely read-only: review, audit, inspect, analyze, explain, standing alone, or when its only write is gitignored runtime state under `.skilled/skills/.state/`. A read-only word next to a write trigger does not disqualify it.\n74: \n75: - **Machine contract:** `system-spec-kit/shared/gate-3-classifier.ts` (`classifyPrompt()`) owns the exact vocabulary; the sentence above paraphrases it.\n76: - **Options (stable labels, recommend one), asked via the `communication-handoff.md` §5 tool:**\n77:   - **A) Existing** - Continue in the detected/current spec or its current phase child when the work fits that scope. **Reply with the folder path.**\n78:   - **B) New** - Create a new top-level packet only when no existing packet suits the work. Decide independently whether it is standard or phased. **Reply with a new folder path.**\n79:   - **C) Related** - Use another existing packet, a child of an existing phase parent, a related standard packet split into phases once it meets both thresholds independently, or a series parent for a different change to the same artifact as an existing same-track packet. **Reply with the folder or child path.**\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 80]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/AGENTS.md\",\"offset\":50,\"limit\":30}"},"time":{"start":179453