→ cite and proceed\\n- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]`\\n- **Artifact trigger — binds on what you write, regardless of the advisor score.**\"}"},"time":{"start":1794531732908,"end":1794531735226}}}}
